# Copy to .env and fill in from the Firebase console (Project settings > Your apps),
# or derive from android/app/google-services.json.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Ads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two switches, and they do different jobs. Confusing them is how you either
# ship with no ads or click your own live ones.
#
#   VITE_ADS_PROVIDER   'admob' runs the real SDK · 'fake' draws a placeholder
#   VITE_ADMOB_TESTING  'true' makes the SDK return TEST ads whatever unit id
#                       you give it — no revenue, no impressions on a live
#                       unit, safe to tap
#
# Google publishes fixed sample unit ids that always return a test ad. Develop
# against those from the start; waiting until release means shipping consent
# and lifecycle code that has never run.
#
#   ca-app-pub-3940256099942544/6300978111   banner
#   ca-app-pub-3940256099942544/1033173712   interstitial
#   ca-app-pub-3940256099942544/5224354917   rewarded
#   ca-app-pub-3940256099942544~3347511713   app id (manifest)
#
# Going live, in this order:
#   1. npm i @capacitor-community/admob && npx cap sync
#   2. AdMob console → add the app → create the three ad units
#   3. put the real unit ids below, and the real app id in
#      android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml (APPLICATION_ID — a tilde, not a slash)
#   4. keep VITE_ADMOB_TESTING=true and check on a device that ads still load.
#      A typo in a unit id fails silently: no ad, no error, no revenue.
#   5. only then set VITE_ADMOB_TESTING=false
#
# ⚠️ Once step 5 is done, never tap an ad in your own build. That is invalid
#    traffic and it is how AdMob accounts get suspended.
VITE_ADS_PROVIDER=fake
VITE_ADMOB_TESTING=true
VITE_ADMOB_BANNER_ID=ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/XXXXXXXXXX
VITE_ADMOB_INTERSTITIAL_ID=ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/XXXXXXXXXX
VITE_ADMOB_REWARDED_ID=ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/XXXXXXXXXX

# ── Billing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 'none' (default) means nothing can be charged, so the Remove Ads entry point
# and screen are both hidden. Keep it on until the product is live: a purchase
# flow that cannot take money hands the product over free and tells the player
# they bought it.
#
# To go live at real release:
#   1. Play Console > in-app product (managed), id `remove_ads_permanent`, activate
#   2. npm i @capacitor-community/in-app-purchases && npx cap sync
#   3. set VITE_BILLING_PROVIDER=play
VITE_BILLING_PROVIDER=none
